From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: reject a HTB leaf that cannot shape anything

airoha_dev_select_queue() steers a net_device's traffic to one fixed QoS
channel, derived from the GDM port id.  The qdisc offset is taken from the
class minor, modulo AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS:

	channel = TC_H_MIN(classid) % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS;

Nothing ties the two together.  On the XR1710G the WAN port is GDM2, so
its only usable channel is 2 and "tc class add dev wan root classid 1:2"
is the sparse one.  The example a reader is most likely to copy,
"classid 1:1", maps to channel 1 instead: the leaf is allocated, the
driver accepts it, tc reports success, the shaper is programmed - and no
packet is ever queued to it.  Traffic runs at full speed with a rate limit
that looks configured, which is the worst possible outcome for a
feature whose entire point is to slow traffic down.

Reject the mismatch with an explicit extack message naming the channel the
device actually uses, so the failure is immediate and self-explaining
rather than silent.

DSA user ports are left alone: the DSA tag selects the channel per packet,
so a single user port has no one channel to compare against.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3327,6 +3394,28 @@
 	struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev = netdev_priv(netdev);
 	struct airoha_qdma *qdma;
 
+	/* airoha_dev_select_queue() sends this net_device's traffic to one
+	 * fixed QoS channel, its GDM port id. A leaf whose classid maps to a
+	 * different channel therefore programs a shaper that nothing feeds:
+	 * tc accepts the qdisc, reports no error, and the traffic runs
+	 * unshaped. WAN is GDM2, so the usual "classid 1:1" example silently
+	 * does nothing while 1:2 is the one that shapes. Refuse the mismatch
+	 * rather than accept it.
+	 *
+	 * DSA user ports have no single channel (the tag selects it per
+	 * packet), so only the non-DSA case is checked here.
+	 */
+	if (!netdev_uses_dsa(netdev) && dev->port &&
+	    channel != dev->port->id % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS) {
+		NL_SET_ERR_MSG_FMT_MOD(opt->extack,
+				       "classid %x:%x maps to QoS channel %u, but %s uses channel %u",
+				       TC_H_MAJ(opt->classid) >> 16,
+				       TC_H_MIN(opt->classid), channel,
+				       netdev_name(netdev),
+				       dev->port->id % AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	/* Here we need to check the requested QDMA channel is not already
 	 * in use by another net_device running on the same QDMA block.
 	 */
